<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ramillies</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1706">1706</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Ramillies · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ramillies was fought on 23 May 1706 near the village of Ramillies in Brabant, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>. An allied army under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-churchill-1st-duke-of-marlborough">Duke of Marlborough</a> routed the French and Bavarian forces of Marshal Villeroi. Within weeks most of the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a>, fell to the allies, who recognised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> claimant Charles III there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ramillies.jpg" alt="Battle of Ramillies" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rijksmuseum · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:De_slag_bij_Ramillies_tussen_de_Fransen_en_de_Geallieerden,_23_mei_1706,_SK-A-4061.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under the Habsburgs Brabant became a main theatre of the Eighty Years' War, with the Spanish Fury at Antwerp in 1576, Alexander Farnese's siege of Antwerp in 1584–1585, and in 1706 the Duke of Marlborough's victory at the <b>Battle of Ramillies</b> gave the allies control of the duchy.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-brabant">Duchy of Brabant · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In the War of the Spanish Succession John Churchill, Duke of Marlborough, won at <b>Ramillies</b> in 1706, Oudenarde in 1708 and Malplaquet in 1709, and the Treaty of Utrecht (1713) gave Britain Gibraltar, Minorca, Newfoundland and Nova Scotia and the asiento to supply enslaved Africans to Spanish America.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-great-britain">Kingdom of Great Britain · Military</a></li></ul></section>
